  "implementation": [
    "Unix standard pipe channels use libuv-sized duplex socket pairs; per-operation nonblocking send/recv preserve blocking descriptors when inherited by another child.",
    "Native output demand and ownership prevent an inherited pipe from being consumed by an eager parent reader. Actual owned descriptors are duplicated for registered stream identities.",
    "Canonical native next-tick retention is shared by JSON IPC and stdio flush scheduling. Reaped children with inactive inherited readers do not keep the parent alive.",
    "Native pipe plans separate legacy end/close destruction and once-only completion from modern Readable EOF and listener lifetimes. Genuine standard streams expose _isStdio."
  ],
